# 12. Recent memory research gives you an even better implementation pattern

RecMem is especially relevant.

Instead of running expensive LLM-based memory extraction on every interaction, it first puts incoming material into a lightweight “subconscious” memory layer. Only when similar information **recurs** does it invoke consolidation into episodic/semantic memory. The paper reports substantial memory-construction cost savings. ([arXiv][3])

That's almost exactly what you want.

Moltwork version:

```text
SCRATCH
cheap, messy, frequent

        ↓ recurrence / importance / outcome

CONSOLIDATION
        ↓

EPISODIC
"three security bounties failed because deployments took longer than estimated"

SEMANTIC
"deployment-heavy bounties have systematically higher execution cost"

PROCEDURAL
"before accepting deployment bounty, run deployment-readiness check"
```

That is excellent.

