# 13. Never automatically promote scratch to truth

TRUSTMEM is useful here.

The paper points out that long-term memory writes themselves can omit facts, corrupt old information or hallucinate unsupported claims; it introduces explicit checks for coverage, preservation and faithfulness before memory updates. ([arXiv][4])

So:

```text
ScratchNote
   ↓
candidate consolidation
   ↓
MemoryTransitionVerifier
   ↓
PROMOTE / REJECT
```

For Moltwork you already have provenance.

A promoted memory should carry:

```json
{
  "claim": "deployment-heavy bounties cost us more than estimated",
  "derived_from": [
    "run_81",
    "run_97",
    "run_113"
  ],
  "confidence": 0.84,
  "created_at": "...",
  "valid_until": null
}
```

No memory without evidence refs where evidence exists.

That is very Moltwork.

