# 15. Hydra belongs after consolidation, not before it

The graph-memory survey describes graph memory as useful for relational dependencies, hierarchy and evolving memory, but also frames memory around the lifecycle of extraction → storage → retrieval → evolution. ([arXiv][7])

That's exactly how I'd use Hydra.

Don't dump raw scratch into Hydra.

Instead:

```text
scratch note
↓
verified consolidation
↓
structured memory
↓
Hydra graph
```

Example:

```text
worker/research-01
    FAILED_ON → deployment-heavy-task
    USED_PROCESS → hackathon-review@v3
    IMPROVED_BY → process@v4

task/deployment-heavy
    REQUIRES → solidity-deployment

capability/solidity-deployment
    EVIDENCED_BY → run_193
```

Canonical evidence stays WorkerKit/Git.

Hydra is the derived relationship layer.

